 "limits": [
  "Yahoo hourly closes are consolidated market data, not the latent reference price of the AMM; they proxy the 24/5 equity reference.",
  "The observation map h is not independently calibrated to real pool prices in this semi-synthetic check; the public bars and feed schedules used here calibrate return/freeze inputs, not a paired full-h estimation sample. The run therefore tests return/freeze calibration, not h external validity.",
  "kappa is a local AR(1) estimate on a nonstationary price level; it is not a structural mean-reversion parameter.",
  "Jump statistics use a fixed 4-sigma threshold and are descriptive; they do not identify a jump-diffusion mixture.",
  "Weekend/holiday gap sd mixes latent price movement with market microstructure at the reopen; it is not a pure de-freeze jump.",
  "The gap sd is measured across the market closure (~65 h on weekends), not the 52--56 h oracle stale interval used as tau; using the longer market duration in the denominator would lower the reported gap ratios, so they are conservative.",
  "Sigma and the AR(1) use bar timestamps as interval starts; the 16:00 bar is after-hours and is excluded from the regular session. The 40--70 h gap bucket is duration-based and can contain midweek holiday closures.",
  "P2's holiday labels include short partial gaps (e.g. 24 h weekday outages inside a holiday week); the table takes the longest gap per labelled holiday to recover the closure."
 ]
